# ─── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The real API key and webhook secret live here. appsettings.json ships with
# an empty key, pointed at the mock and disarmed.
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.Local.json
*.local.json
.env
.env.*
secrets.json
*whsec*
webhook-secret.txt
*.pem
*.key

# ─── Data and generated documents ────────────────────────────────────────
# Real party names, addresses and signatures. Never commit these.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
storage/
src/EDrafter.Api/storage/

# Generated and downloaded PDFs
lease-agreement.pdf
signed-agreement.pdf
test-2page.pdf
src/*.pdf
/*.pdf

# ─── Commercial and contractual documents ────────────────────────────────
# eDrafter's negotiated rates and the signed contract with VSoftware
# Consulting. They stay on disk; they do not belong in source control.
Proposal & Quotation*.pdf
*Service Agreement*.docx
eDrafter-B2B-API-Documentation.pdf

# Postman collection and environment — internal working files.
*.postman_collection.json
*.postman_environment.json

# ─── Working notes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Most of docs/ is the research trail: pricing negotiations, questions put to
# eDrafter, draft emails, superseded plans. Only three files describe the
# system as it stands, and those are the three that ship.
#
#   13-API-EXAMPLES.md      every endpoint, with a working request
#   18-THE-FLOW.md          what the system does
#   19-SETUP-AND-CONFIG.md  how to run it, configure it, register webhooks
#   21-WEBHOOKS.md          registering and testing the eDrafter + Zoho webhooks
#   22-HOW-TO-RUN.md        running it, what costs money, endpoints
docs/*
!docs/13-API-EXAMPLES.md
!docs/18-THE-FLOW.md
!docs/19-SETUP-AND-CONFIG.md
!docs/21-WEBHOOKS.md
!docs/22-HOW-TO-RUN.md

